The deliberation remains divided between 23 and 10, centering on whether the prompt's "95% confidence" requirement mandates a formal 5% hypothesis test on the concentration parameter or corresponds to the canonical weak-instrument heuristic. By applying the Nagar asymptotic approximation to determine the threshold non-centrality parameter ($\mu^2 \ge 10$) and computing the 95th percentile critical value of the resulting non-central distribution with 1 degree of freedom, one obtains $F = (\sqrt{10} + 1.645)^2 \approx 23.11$. Consequently, 23 remains the most mathematically consistent answer under the prompt's explicit assumptions.
}

